PHASE H  --  prime-power versus mixed-prime split of the arithmetic side
============================================================================================

[FACT] f = E * M with E = prod_p exp(sum_k (b_{p^k}/(k log p)) p^{-ks})
     From -f'/f = sum b_n n^{-s} and log f = sum c_n n^{-s} one gets
     c_n = b_n / log n, so  log f(s) = sum_{n>=2} (b_n / log n) n^{-s}.  Splitting
     that series by the support of n gives log E and log M; log E is supported on
     prime powers, hence E = prod_p (local factor) is an Euler product BY
     CONSTRUCTION, and f = E * M.

